<title>GEORGIA: SOCCER-GEORGIAN LEAGUE TITLE WINNERS SINCE 1990.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GEORGIAN LEAGUE TITLE WINNERS SINCE 1990.</headline>
<dateline>TBILISI 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dynamo Tbilisi, who secured their</p>
<p>sixth successive league and cup double on Monday, have won all</p>
<p>eight Georgian league titles since the championship was founded.</p>
<p>The following are the winners and runners-up since Georgia</p>
<p>broke away from Soviet soccer in 1990 (1990 season</p>
<p>March-November, 1991 March-June, 1991-92 onwards August-June):</p>
<p>		Champions			 Runners-up</p>
<p> 1990	 Dynamo Tbilisi		  Guria Lanchkhuti</p>
<p> 1991	 Dynamo Tbilisi		  Guria Lanchkhuti</p>
<p> 1991-92    Dynamo Tbilisi		  Tskhumi Sukhumi</p>
<p> 1992-93    Dynamo Tbilisi		  Shevardeni-1906 Tbilisi</p>
<p> 1993-94    Dynamo Tbilisi		  Kolkheti-1913 Poti</p>
<p> 1994-95    Dynamo Tbilisi		  Samtredia</p>
<p> 1995-96    Dynamo Tbilisi		  Margveti Zestafoni</p>
<p> 1996-97    Dynamo Tbilisi		  To be decided</p>
<p>Dynamo Tbilisi won the Soviet championship in 1964 and 1978,</p>
<p>the only Georgian club ever to do so in the 55-year history of</p>
<p>the Soviet league from 1936 to 1991.</p>
</text>
